 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Choosing a type",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All nine types share the 1.0 A average and 25 A surge ratings and the 90.0 °C/W thermal resistance. Maximum forward voltage at 1 A takes four values with voltage class (0.55, 0.70, 0.85 and 0.9 V), the 25 °C leakage limit three (0.3, 0.2 and 0.1 mA), and typical capacitance two: 110 pF for SS12 to SS14, 80 pF for SS15 to SS1200. VRMS is 0.7 × VRRM and VDC equals VRRM."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Full 1.0 A average current is allowed up to a case temperature of 100 °C; above that the rating falls linearly to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Leakage and temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Typical reverse current from near zero to full rated reverse voltage is about 1.2 to 4.1 µA at TJ = 25 °C, 63 to 340 µA at 75 °C and 420 to 3000 µA at 100 °C, climbing fastest over the top fifth of the voltage range. The SS12 to SS16 group lies above the SS18 to SS1200 group at each temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge over several cycles",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 25 A surge limit applies to one 60 Hz half-cycle; over a train of cycles the limit falls, to about 13.5 A at 10 cycles and about 6.3 A at 100."
  }
 ],
